 117:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 118:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** /** @defgroup RCC_Exported_Functions_Group1 Initialization and de-initialization functions 
 119:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *  @brief    Initialization and Configuration functions 
 120:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *
 121:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   @verbatim    
 122:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ===============================================================================
 123:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****            ##### Initialization and de-initialization functions #####
 124:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ===============================================================================
 125:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..]
 126:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****       This section provides functions allowing to configure the internal/external oscillators
 127:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (HSE, HSI, LSE, LSI, PLL, CSS and MCO) and the System buses clocks (SYSCLK, AHB, APB1
 128:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****       and APB2).
 129:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 130:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..] Internal/external clock and PLL configuration
 131:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) HSI (high-speed internal), 8 MHz factory-trimmed RC used directly or through
 132:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           the PLL as System clock source.
 133:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           The HSI clock can be used also to clock the USART and I2C peripherals.
 134:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 135:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) LSI (low-speed internal), ~40 KHz low consumption RC used as IWDG and/or RTC
 136:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           clock source.
 137:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 138:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) HSE (high-speed external), 4 to 32 MHz crystal oscillator used directly or
 139:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           through the PLL as System clock source. Can be used also as RTC clock source.
 140:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 141:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) LSE (low-speed external), 32 KHz oscillator used as RTC clock source.   
 142:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 143:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) PLL (clocked by HSI or HSE), featuring different output clocks:
 144:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) The first output is used to generate the high speed system clock (up to 72 MHz)
ARM GAS  /tmp/cccxcDip.s 			page 4


 145:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) The second output is used to generate the clock for the USB FS (48 MHz)
 146:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) The third output may be used to generate the clock for the ADC peripherals (up to 72 M
 147:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) The fourth output may be used to generate the clock for the TIM peripherals (144 MHz)
 148:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 149:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) CSS (Clock security system), once enable using the macro __HAL_RCC_CSS_ENABLE()
 150:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           and if a HSE clock failure occurs(HSE used directly or through PLL as System 
 151:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           clock source), the System clocks automatically switched to HSI and an interrupt
 152:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           is generated if enabled. The interrupt is linked to the Cortex-M4 NMI 
 153:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           (Non-Maskable Interrupt) exception vector.   
 154:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 155:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) MCO (microcontroller clock output), used to output SYSCLK, HSI, HSE, LSI, LSE or PLL
 156:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           clock (divided by 2) output on pin (such as PA8 pin).
 157:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 158:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..] System, AHB and APB buses clocks configuration
 159:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) Several clock sources can be used to drive the System clock (SYSCLK): HSI,
 160:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           HSE and PLL.
 161:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           The AHB clock (HCLK) is derived from System clock through configurable
 162:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           prescaler and used to clock the CPU, memory and peripherals mapped
 163:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           on AHB bus (DMA, GPIO...). APB1 (PCLK1) and APB2 (PCLK2) clocks are derived
 164:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           from AHB clock through configurable prescalers and used to clock
 165:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           the peripherals mapped on these buses. You can use
 166:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****           "HAL_RCC_GetSysClockFreq()" function to retrieve the frequencies of these clocks.
 167:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 168:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (#) All the peripheral clocks are derived from the System clock (SYSCLK) except:
 169:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) The FLASH program/erase clock  which is always HSI 8MHz clock.
 170:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) The USB 48 MHz clock which is derived from the PLL VCO clock.
 171:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) The USART clock which can be derived as well from HSI 8MHz, LSI or LSE.
 172:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) The I2C clock which can be derived as well from HSI 8MHz clock.
 173:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) The ADC clock which is derived from PLL output.
 174:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) The RTC clock which is derived from the LSE, LSI or 1 MHz HSE_RTC
 175:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****              (HSE divided by a programmable prescaler). The System clock (SYSCLK)
 176:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****              frequency must be higher or equal to the RTC clock frequency.
 177:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****         (++) IWDG clock which is always the LSI clock.
 178:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 179:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) For the STM32F3xx devices, the maximum frequency of the SYSCLK, HCLK, PCLK1 and PCLK2 
 180:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****              Depending on the SYSCLK frequency, the flash latency should be adapted accordingly.
 181:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 182:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****          (#) After reset, the System clock source is the HSI (8 MHz) with 0 WS and
 183:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****              prefetch is disabled.
 184:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   @endverbatim
