 670:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
 671:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c **** /**
 672:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @brief  Initializes the CPU, AHB and APB buses clocks according to the specified 
 673:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *         parameters in the RCC_ClkInitStruct.
 674:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @param  RCC_ClkInitStruct pointer to an RCC_OscInitTypeDef structure that
 675:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *         contains the configuration information for the RCC peripheral.
 676:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @param  FLatency FLASH Latency                   
 677:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *          The value of this parameter depend on device used within the same series
 678:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @note   The SystemCoreClock CMSIS variable is used to store System Clock Frequency 
 679:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *         and updated by @ref HAL_RCC_GetHCLKFreq() function called within this function
 680:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *
 681:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @note   The HSI is used (enabled by hardware) as system clock source after
 682:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *         start-up from Reset, wake-up from STOP and STANDBY mode, or in case
 683:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *         of failure of the HSE used directly or indirectly as system clock
 684:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *         (if the Clock Security System CSS is enabled).
 685:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *           
 686:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   * @note   A switch from one clock source to another occurs only if the target
 687:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *         clock source is ready (clock stable after start-up delay or PLL locked). 
 688:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *         If a clock source which is not yet ready is selected, the switch will
 689:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *         occur when the clock source will be ready. 
 690:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *         You can use @ref HAL_RCC_GetClockConfig() function to know which clock is
 691:Inc/STM32F3xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f3xx_hal_rcc.c ****   *         currently used as system clock source.
